# BuildKit per-Dockerfile ignore for Dockerfile.hw (paths relative to the build
# context root, /home/swarm/code). Allowlist style: ship ONLY the four source
# trees the hw image needs; everything else under code/ stays on the host.
*
!mighty_ws/src
!decomp_ws/src
# livox_ros_driver2 is baked PREBUILT (its fork source no longer builds against the
# v1.2.5 SDK on this box) — ship its colcon install tree, not the source.
!livox_ws/install
!Livox-SDK2

# Sim-only source repos: not part of the hw package closure and mighty builds
# with -DBUILD_SIMULATION=OFF, so keep them out of the image entirely.
# EXCEPTION: local_sensing (+ its quadrotor_msgs dep) must exist because
# onboard_mighty.launch.py calls get_package_share_directory('local_sensing')
# unconditionally at parse time, even on hardware.
mighty_ws/src/gazebo_ros_pkgs
mighty_ws/src/livox_laser_simulation_ros2
mighty_ws/src/realsense_gazebo_plugin
mighty_ws/src/uav_simulator
!mighty_ws/src/uav_simulator/local_sensing
!mighty_ws/src/uav_simulator/Utils/quadrotor_msgs

# Junk. NOTE: mighty's benchmarking/, worlds/, meshes/, urdf/ MUST ship — they
# are referenced by install() rules in mighty's CMakeLists.
**/.git
**/__pycache__
**/*.ipynb
Livox-SDK2/build

# RR04-specific: mighty_ws/src here still carries a DUPLICATE DecompROS2 (the 4
# decomp packages are built separately from decomp_ws/src) and a non-colcon
# Livox-SDK2 dir. Keep both out of the image build context to avoid a decomp
# double-build/conflict and stray host artifacts.
mighty_ws/src/DecompROS2
mighty_ws/src/Livox-SDK2
